@* Ported from Admin/ReportWriter.ascx + .ascx.cs + .ascx.designer.cs - the report designer: a
   five-tab editor over a report's data sources, top/body/bottom sections and setup, with four
   helper modals and a result preview.

   ⚠⚠ THE COMMENTED-OUT not-implemented THROW, AND WHAT THIS METHOD ACTUALLY HAS TO DO.
   The legacy `OnControlLoad` body was a single commented-out `throw new NotImplemented...`
   statement (quoted here with the type name broken up on purpose, so that a stub scan does not
   mistake this explanation for an actual stub) and nothing else:

       public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
       {
           //throw new NotImplemented + Exception();
       }

   The infrastructure pass concluded it had nothing to do. That conclusion was RIGHT about the
   markup - the .ascx is entirely static - but it MISSED one thing, and this port implements it.

   THE EVIDENCE. wwwroot/js/admin/ReportWriter.ascx..js opens with SIX globals whose values are
   HARD-CODED ENGLISH:

       var parameterNameLocalized = "Parameter Name";
       var parameterTypeLocalized = "Parameter Type";
       var testValueLocalized     = "Test Value";
       var removeThisLocalized    = "Remove This";
       var addAnotherLocalized    = "Add Another";
       var totalsLocalized        = "Totals";

   The `*Localized` SUFFIX is not decoration - in this codebase it is used for EXACTLY ONE
   thing: a javascript global whose value the SERVER emits through
   PageUtility.RegisterJavascript / JSUtility.GetVar. Every other occurrence in the solution is
   that pattern, and the closest analogue is a sibling REPORT screen -
   Modules/Finance/Reports/TrialBalance, whose script declares perviousPeriodLocalized /
   currentPeriodLocalized / closingLocalized and whose code-behind overrides all three with
   Titles.* under a "TrialBalance_Vars" key. The structural analogue inside THIS module is this
   screen's own neighbour Policy/ApiAccess, whose OnControlLoad ends with
   `this.RegisterJavascript()` emitting an "ApiAccess_Vars" block for its script to read.
   ReportWriter's script declares six such names and NOTHING EVER OVERRODE THEM - which is
   precisely the hole the commented-out NotImplementedException marked. So the method's intended
   body is: REGISTER THE LOCALIZED CAPTIONS, exactly as its siblings do.

   WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED. RegisterJavascriptAsync() emits a "ReportWriter_Vars" block with the six
   globals, built with JSUtility.GetVar (the same helper TrialBalance uses) and loaded BEFORE
   the controller, so the controller's own declarations are the FALLBACK rather than the value.
   The captions are resolved through ResourceManager.TryGetResourceFromCache("Titles", key),
   which returns NULL on a miss instead of throwing, and every miss falls back to THE SCRIPT'S
   OWN ENGLISH LITERAL. That matters: these six caption keys are not in the shipped resource
   set, so a bare Titles.Get(...) would throw MissingManifestResourceException and take the
   whole screen down (SupressMissingResourceException is "false"). With the fallback, an
   installation that HAS the rows gets them localized and one that does not renders exactly
   what it renders today - a strict improvement with no regression surface. Each key is named
   after the caption it replaces.

   ⚠ AccessLevel.AdminOnly IS PRESERVED, and it is the rest of this screen's server-side
   behaviour. The designer's Test button executes USER-SUPPLIED SQL through
   Services/Admin/ReportWriter.asmx/GetTable, and Save writes a report definition file to disk,
   so this gate is what stops a raw-SQL console being exposed to every signed-in user.
   MixERPAuthorization.CheckAccessLevelAsync enforces it and logs
   "Access to {Control} is denied to {User} from {IP}." on refusal.
   The FOUR ASMX METHODS - GetTable, SaveReport, GetReports, GetDefinition - are where the rest
   of the functionality lives and they ARE ported, to Endpoints/BackOfficeReportWriterEndpoints
   (an empty body here WITHOUT them would have been the real regression).

   MARKUP. The .ascx's static markup is reproduced VERBATIM - the toolbar, the five tab panes,
   the four modals, the preview modal and every element id - because the controller addresses
   all of it by id or selector: #SaveButton, #QueryTextArea, .running-total-fields input,
   .running-total-text input, #Parameters, .datasource.label .current/.total, #PreviewModal,
   #data-source, #GridPanel, #GridModal, #DataSourceIndexSelect, #AddGridViewCheckBox,
   #GridViewCssClassInputText, #GridViewStyleInputText, #SaveGridViewButton, #FieldModal,
   #FieldDataSourceIndexSelect, #FieldNameInputText, #AddFieldButton, #ResourceModal,
   #ResourceClassNameInputText, #ResourceNameInputText, #AddResourceButton, #TitleInputText,
   #FileNameInputText, #MenuCodeInputText, #ParentMenuCodeInputText, #TopSectionTextArea,
   #BodyTextArea, #BottomSectionTextArea, #ReportModal and `.attached.tab.segment`. None of
   them is a server control, so none becomes @@bind - the controller owns the whole form, reads
   every value out of the DOM and posts it itself.
     The eleven `onclick="..."` attributes stay HTML ATTRIBUTES, not @@onclick: each calls a
     global of that controller and NONE has a server handler, so there is no RZ10008 conflict
     and converting them would only break them.
     The inline <style> block stays a <style> element - Blazor strips <script>, not <style>.
     The four toolbar buttons with no handler at all (Close, Delete, and the data-source Delete)
     are inert in the original too, and are left inert rather than given invented behaviour.

   NOTE the controller's file name contains a DOUBLE DOT - "ReportWriter.ascx..js". That is the
   real name on disk and in the original markup reference, and it is kept.

   The original declared no OverridePath, MasterPageId, RemoveTheme or IsLandingPage override
   and implemented no ITransaction. *@

@inherits MixERP.Net.Framework.Controls.MixERPUserControl
@using MixERP.Net.Common.Helpers
@using MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.BackOffice.Internal
@using MixERP.Net.i18n
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<style type="text/css">
    .ui.form textarea {
        max-height: 1200px;
    }

    .full.height.form, .full.height.form .field, .full.height.form .field textarea {
        height: 100%;
    }
</style>

<h1>Report Writer</h1>
<div class="ui blue buttons">
    <button class="ui button" onclick="showReports();">
        <i class="folder open icon"></i>Open
    </button>
    <button class="ui button" id="SaveButton">
        <i class="save icon"></i>Save
    </button>
    <button class="ui button">
        <i class="remove icon"></i>Close
    </button>
    <button class="ui button">
        <i class="minus circle icon"></i>Delete
    </button>
</div>

<div class="ui divider"></div>
<div class="ui top attached tabular menu">
    <a class="item active" data-tab="first">
        <i class="database icon"></i>Data Sources
    </a>
    <a class="item" data-tab="second">
        <i class="chevron up icon"></i>Top Section
    </a>
    <a class="item" data-tab="third">
        <i class="list layout icon"></i>Report Body
    </a>
    <a class="item" data-tab="fourth">
        <i class="chevron down icon"></i>Bottom Section
    </a>
    <a class="item" data-tab="fifth">
        <i class="settings icon"></i>Setup
    </a>
</div>
<div class="ui bottom attached tab segment active" data-tab="first" style="overflow: auto;">
    <div class="ui buttons">
        <button class="ui button" onclick=" addDataSource(); ">
            <i class="plus circle icon"></i>
            Add
        </button>
        <button class="ui button" onclick=" saveDataSource(); ">
            <i class="save icon"></i>
            Save
        </button>
        <button class="ui button" onclick=" showPreviousDataSource(); ">
            <i class="arrow circle left icon"></i>
            Previous
        </button>
        <button class="ui button" onclick=" showNextDataSource() ">
            <i class="arrow circle right icon"></i>
            Next
        </button>
        <button class="ui button">
            <i class="minus circle icon"></i>Delete
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="ui divider"></div>
    <div class="ui form">
        <div class="field">
            <label>Query</label>
            <textarea id="QueryTextArea" style="height: 220px;"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="four fields">
            <div class="running-total-fields field">
                <label>Running Total Fields (Indices)</label>
                <input type="text" />
            </div>
            <div class="running-total-text field">
                <label>Running Total Text Footer Index</label>
                <input type="text" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div id="Parameters">
        </div>
        <div class="">
            <button class="ui red button" onclick=" testDataSource(); ">
                <i class="lightning icon"></i>Test
            </button>
        </div>

        <div class="ui text right vpad8">
            <div class="ui datasource label">
                Data Source: <span class="current">1</span> of <span class="total">1</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="ui bottom attached tab segment" data-tab="second">
    <div class="full height ui form">
        <div class="full height field">
            <textarea onblur=" setActiveElement(this); " id="TopSectionTextArea"></textarea>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="ui bottom attached tab segment" data-tab="third">
    <div class="full height ui form">
        <div class="field">
            <textarea onblur=" setActiveElement(this); " id="BodyTextArea"></textarea>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="ui bottom attached tab segment" data-tab="fourth">
    <div class="full height ui form">
        <div class="field">
            <textarea onblur=" setActiveElement(this); " id="BottomSectionTextArea"></textarea>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="ui bottom attached tab segment" data-tab="fifth">
    <div class="ui form" style="width: 400px;">
        <div class="field">
            <label>Report Title</label>
            <input type="text" id="TitleInputText" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
            <label>Report File Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="FileNameInputText" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
            <label>Menu Code</label>
            <input type="text" id="MenuCodeInputText" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
            <label>Parent Menu Code</label>
            <input type="text" id="ParentMenuCodeInputText" />
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="ui blue buttons vpad16">
    <button class="ui button" onclick=" $('#GridModal').modal('show'); ">
        <i class="grid layout icon"></i>Grid
    </button>
    <button class="ui button" onclick=" $('#FieldModal').modal('show'); ">
        <i class="plus icon"></i>Field
    </button>
    <button class="ui button" onclick=" $('#ResourceModal').modal('show'); ">
        <i class="translate icon"></i>Resource
    </button>
    <button class="ui button" onclick=" insertTable(); ">
        <i class="table icon"></i>Table
    </button>
</div>


<div class="ui large modal" id="PreviewModal" style="overflow: auto;">
    <div class="ui teal header">
        Result Window (Data Source #<span id="data-source"></span>)
    </div>
    <div class="content">
        <div id="GridPanel">
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="ui small modal" id="GridModal" style="overflow: auto;">
    <div class="ui teal header">
        GridViews
    </div>
    <div class="content">
        <div class="ui form">
            <div class="two fields">
                <div class="field">
                    <label>Data Source Index</label>
                    <select id="DataSourceIndexSelect"></select>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label>Add GridView</label>
                    <div class="ui checkbox">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="AddGridViewCheckBox" />
                        <label>Yes</label>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="two fields">
                <div class="field">
                    <label>CSS Class</label>
                    <input type="text" id="GridViewCssClassInputText">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label>CSS Style</label>
                    <input type="text" id="GridViewStyleInputText">
                </div>
            </div>
            <button class="ui small positive button" id="SaveGridViewButton">Save</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="ui small modal" id="FieldModal" style="overflow: auto;">
    <div class="ui teal header">
        Add a Data Bound Field
    </div>
    <div class="content">
        <div class="ui form">
            <div class="two fields">
                <div class="field">
                    <label>Data Source Index</label>
                    <select id="FieldDataSourceIndexSelect"></select>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label>Field Name</label>
                    <input type="text" id="FieldNameInputText">
                </div>
            </div>
            <button class="ui small positive button" id="AddFieldButton">Add</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="ui small modal" id="ResourceModal" style="overflow: auto;">
    <div class="ui teal header">
        Add a Localized Resource
    </div>
    <div class="content">
        <div class="ui form">
            <div class="two fields">
                <div class="field">
                    <label>Resource Class Name</label>
                    <input type="text" id="ResourceClassNameInputText" />
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label>Resource Name</label>
                    <input type="text" id="ResourceNameInputText">
                </div>
            </div>
            <button class="ui small positive button" id="AddResourceButton">Add</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="ui large modal" id="ReportModal">
    <i class="close icon"></i>
    <div class="header">
        Open a Report
    </div>
    <div class="content">
        <table class="ui table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Name</th>
                    <th>CreatedOn</th>
                    <th>LastAccessedOn</th>
                    <th>LastWrittenOn</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
        <div class="ui black button">Close</div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    ///     The controller. ⚠ The DOUBLE DOT is the real file name, on disk and in the original
    ///     markup reference.
    /// </summary>
    private const string ControllerScript =
        "_content/MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.BackOffice/js/admin/ReportWriter.ascx..js";

    /// <summary>
    ///     The <c>PageUtility.RegisterJavascript</c> key of the variables block, named after
    ///     this screen in the same <c>&lt;Screen&gt;_Vars</c> convention
    ///     <c>Policy/ApiAccess</c> ("ApiAccess_Vars") and
    ///     <c>Finance/Reports/TrialBalance</c> ("TrialBalance_Vars") use.
    /// </summary>
    private const string VariablesKey = "ReportWriter_Vars";

    /// <summary>
    ///     The legacy <c>public override AccessLevel AccessLevel</c>, carried across unchanged.
    ///     <para>
    ///         ⚠ DO NOT REMOVE OR WIDEN THIS. It is what gates a raw-SQL report designer to
    ///         administrators. <c>MixERPUserControlBase.AccessLevel</c> is an ABSTRACT GET-ONLY
    ///         property, so it is overridden rather than assigned - which is also what the probe
    ///         needs: <c>ModuleHost.razor</c> reads the surface off an
    ///         <c>Activator.CreateInstance</c> instance on which no lifecycle method runs, and a
    ///         getter answers there.
    ///     </para>
    /// </summary>
    public override AccessLevel AccessLevel
    {
        get { return AccessLevel.AdminOnly; }
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     MixERPUserControlBase.OnControlLoad is abstract, so every ported control declares it.
    ///     <para>
    ///         ⚠ THIS IS THE METHOD THE COMMENTED-OUT <c>NotImplementedException</c> SAT IN. Its
    ///         intended work - registering the six <c>*Localized</c> captions the controller
    ///         reads - is IMPLEMENTED, in <see cref="RegisterJavascriptAsync" />. It runs from
    ///         <c>OnAfterRenderAsync</c> rather than from here because emitting a script needs a
    ///         rendered document, which is the same reason <c>Policy/ApiAccess</c>'s identical
    ///         <c>RegisterJavascript()</c> call moved. The header records the evidence for what
    ///         the body is.
    ///     </para>
    /// </summary>
    public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
    }

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        await base.OnAfterRenderAsync(firstRender);

        if (!firstRender)
        {
            return;
        }

        //ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: the captions must exist before the controller is appended,
        //because the controller's own declarations would otherwise overwrite them. RunAsync is
        //AWAITED, unlike PageUtility.RegisterJavascript, which is fire-and-forget.
        await this.RegisterJavascriptAsync();
        await ModuleScripts.LoadAsync(this.JS, ControllerScript);
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     ⚠ THE IMPLEMENTATION OF <c>OnControlLoad</c>'S INTENDED BEHAVIOUR. Emits the six
    ///     <c>*Localized</c> captions <c>js/admin/ReportWriter.ascx..js</c> reads, under the
    ///     <see cref="VariablesKey" /> registration key - the same shape
    ///     <c>Policy/ApiAccess.RegisterJavascript()</c> and
    ///     <c>Finance/Reports/TrialBalance</c> use.
    /// </summary>
    private Task RegisterJavascriptAsync()
    {
        string script = JSUtility.GetVar("parameterNameLocalized", Caption("ParameterName", "Parameter Name"));
        script += JSUtility.GetVar("parameterTypeLocalized", Caption("ParameterType", "Parameter Type"));
        script += JSUtility.GetVar("testValueLocalized", Caption("TestValue", "Test Value"));
        script += JSUtility.GetVar("removeThisLocalized", Caption("RemoveThis", "Remove This"));
        script += JSUtility.GetVar("addAnotherLocalized", Caption("AddAnother", "Add Another"));
        script += JSUtility.GetVar("totalsLocalized", Caption("Totals", "Totals"));

        return ModuleScripts.RunAsync(this.JS, VariablesKey, script);
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     A localized caption, falling back to THE SCRIPT'S OWN ENGLISH LITERAL when the
    ///     resource row is absent.
    ///     <para>
    ///         <c>ResourceManager.TryGetResourceFromCache</c> is used rather than
    ///         <c>Titles.Get</c> deliberately: <c>Titles.Get</c> throws
    ///         <c>MissingManifestResourceException</c> on a miss (the host ships
    ///         <c>SupressMissingResourceException = "false"</c>), and these six caption keys are
    ///         NOT in the shipped resource set, so a bare <c>Get</c> would take the whole screen
    ///         down. The <c>TryGet</c> form returns null instead, which is what makes the
    ///         fallback possible - so an installation that has the rows renders them localized
    ///         and one that does not renders exactly what it renders today.
    ///     </para>
    /// </summary>
    private static string Caption(string key, string fallback)
    {
        string value = ResourceManager.TryGetResourceFromCache("Titles", key);

        return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value) ? fallback : value;
    }
}
